message: "If you use these papers, please cite the archived Zenodo releases below."
title: "The Unique Games Theorem: a short self-contained proof and a compressed presentation of OpenAI's proof (papers, LaTeX sources and Lean check logs)"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23265572
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23265572"
abstract: >-
  Two expository preprints on OpenAI's proof of the Unique Games Theorem (23 September 2026),
  with their LaTeX sources and the script and logs of a Comparator check of OpenAI's Lean 4
  formalization of the source theorem. The short proof is self-contained apart from three
  earlier theorems stated as inputs (Håstad's parity gap, the Khot–Minzer–Safra Grassmann
  expansion theorem and Dinur–Steurer projection-game repetition) and simplifies several
  steps of the source; a companion note lists every departure and its credits. The
  compressed presentation follows the source closely. Both were prepared with AI models and
  checked by separate AI reviewers; no human expert has reviewed them. The Lean check
  concerns OpenAI's formal development, not these papers.
